WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:06.900
MICHAEL BALDWIN: Hi, everyone.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.290
I'm Michael Baldwin.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:11.040
I'm a group product manager
in Google Cloud, focused

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.470
on AI and industry solutions.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:16.230
My team leads product management
across several of our priority

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.190
industries.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.090
Thanks for joining us today.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:21.660
The pandemic has clearly
caused a tremendous amount

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.580
of rapid change for all of us.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.380
Today, I want to
speak about ways

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.870
that artificial intelligence
has helped enterprises

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.563
adapt to those changes.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.980
Today I'll cover
trends that we're

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.530
seeing as we work with
our customers, the impact

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:37.530
on key industries, and
how AI can be helpful

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.980
in these moments of change, with
some specific examples of how

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.260
Google Cloud has helped.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.690
As we monitor our own
business, and especially as we

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.820
partner closely
with our customers,

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:51.180
there's a number of common
themes related to the pandemic.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.280
First, a number
of industries are

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.620
seeing significant
shifts in demand,

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.780
along with increased volatility.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:00.870
Second, with this uncertainty
comes cost pressures

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.740
for many businesses.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:04.830
And as these businesses
adapt, they often

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.900
face supply chain uncertainties.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.860
In some cases, suppliers
may be disrupted themselves

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.240
by the pandemic.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.430
In other cases, they may
be struggling to keep up

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:15.890
with spikes in demand.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:18.600
And across the board, it's
becoming much more difficult

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.060
to accurately forecast.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.160
Customer support
cases have risen,

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.790
with channels like call
centers getting overwhelmed,

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:28.530
and virtual work has become
the new normal for many of us

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:31.010
as people continue
to social distance.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.080
And across the board, from
retail to banking to media

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.240
and beyond, we're
seeing companies

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.090
accelerate their digital
transformation initiatives.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:41.190
And today, I'll talk
to you about how

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:46.200
AI is helping with these
digital transformations.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.020
IDC recently said, "no
doubt, the pandemic

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.960
is impacting how every industry
is conducting business,

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:55.810
in some industries AI spend
will actually increase."

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:57.400
Why is this happening?

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.790
Well, we think the benefits
of AI in the industries

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:01.560
that we'll talk
about today are going

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.440
to be amplified by the
pandemic, as we'll discuss

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.700
in detail in the next section.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.539
So there are six industries
that I'll talk through today.

00:02:10.539 --> 00:02:15.205
Retail and CPG, financial
services, manufacturing, health

00:02:15.205 --> 00:02:18.180
care and life sciences, media,
entertainment and gaming,

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.790
and the public sector.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:22.850
So first let's
start with retail.

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.520
We're all consumers of
retail in one way or another.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:28.530
Retailers have seen
massive shifts in demand.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.980
There's overwhelming
demand for food and drug,

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.740
while specialty and department
stores and non essentials are

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:36.080
experiencing declining demand.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.480
There's increased need for
visibility into supply chains

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:43.250
and added need to quickly
replenish in demand items.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:46.220
Also, it's much harder now
to rely on historical data

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.080
for demand forecasting.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.850
In addition,
retailers need to be

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:51.590
able to handle an
increase in returns

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:54.290
from e-commerce channels,
and be able to adapt

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.480
to using their stores
as distribution centers,

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.440
for fulfillment through buy
online and pickup in store.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.320
We also see an acceleration
in digital-first customer

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.800
journeys, in some cases, an
abrupt shift from in-store

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:10.340
to online purchasing that puts a
strain on e-commerce platforms,

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:13.930
fulfillment operations, and
customer service and support.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:15.970
Finally, during these
difficult times,

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:17.560
some retailers
are closing stores

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.570
and are hyper focused
on expense reduction

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:21.730
to preserve liquidity.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:25.120
As COVID-19 accelerates the
transformation to digital,

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:27.130
retailers are looking
for more tools

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:30.400
to personalize experiences
and sell online.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.650
Google Cloud's
Recommendations AI solution

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:35.950
can help retailers adapt to the
changing environment by helping

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:38.740
them sell the right
product at the right time

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:40.630
to the right customer.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:44.230
As an example of this, one of
our customers, Digitec Galaxus,

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:46.300
saw a 40% increase
in click-through rate

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.560
compared to a previous period.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:53.230
Next, let's talk about
financial services.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:56.500
In banking, digital banking
has increased rapidly

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:01.000
from 63% in 2019 to 72% today.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.690
When we look at insurance,
almost 50% of insurance agents

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:06.760
cited building new
customer relationships

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:10.620
remotely as the biggest
challenge during COVID-19.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.840
In the payments industry,
nearly 80% of consumers

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:16.399
use contactless payments today.

00:04:16.399 --> 00:04:19.720
And finally, the financial
services industry as a whole

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:22.810
is facing new and
creative types of fraud.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:25.180
The dollar value of attempted
fraudulent transactions

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:28.678
grew 35% in April,
year over year.

00:04:28.678 --> 00:04:30.220
We've been working
with our customers

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:33.100
using our Document AI
technology to help.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.480
For example, with
mortgage rates low,

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.690
there's a surge in
mortgage applications.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:41.470
Using Document AI, we've created
a bundle of specialized models

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:44.603
focused on specific document
types used in lending,

00:04:44.603 --> 00:04:46.270
and are working with
lenders to speed up

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:48.400
the processing of
paper-intensive mortgage

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.010
applications.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.480
Also, when the US Congress
authorized the Paycheck

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:55.720
Protection Program, or
PPP, earlier this year,

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:58.210
we made the same technology
available to help

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.785
with the processing
of PPP loans.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.640
Next, in manufacturing, like
in many of these industries,

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:07.560
there's increased
cost pressures.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:09.510
Also, workforce
capacity is expected

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:12.540
to decline due to things
like age, absenteeism,

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.970
skill shortage, and
economic pressures,

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:17.600
all accelerated by COVID-19.

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:19.920
The pandemic has brought
about an increased focus

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.020
on safety and health mandates.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:24.390
And finally, as many
of these manufacturers

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:27.210
are supporting the supply chains
of these other industries,

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:31.080
they themselves are facing
unpredictable demand cycles.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:34.080
An example of how Cloud AI is
helping related to the safety

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.150
and health mandates
that I mentioned earlier

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:39.820
is how our Vision API can
be used for worker safety.

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:44.790
The Cloud Vision API uses AI to
detect objects, motions, text,

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:46.800
and more to help
derive insights.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.480
So for this example,
it can be used

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.670
to detect essential
protective gear,

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:55.140
including hard hats, gloves,
face masks and goggles.

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:00.190
Also, it can be used to
detect distancing compliance

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:02.080
from other workers in
close environments,

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:06.655
and to monitor proximity to
machinery in hazardous sites.

00:06:06.655 --> 00:06:08.030
The health care
industry has been

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:10.322
on the front lines of many
of the pressures and changes

00:06:10.322 --> 00:06:12.140
brought about by the pandemic.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:14.450
Large health system
saw revenue plummet

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:16.700
in areas like elective care.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:18.620
And elective care has
been slowly resuming

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:22.340
after a 10-week hiatus, however
smaller hospitals in some cases

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:24.520
are struggling to stay open.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:27.100
Providers are beginning
to embrace telehealth

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:29.670
with many visits now
being conducted virtually.

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:32.860
And this is a trend that we
expect to largely persist.

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:35.900
Payers have seen a surge
in COVID-19 claims,

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:37.900
however these have been
offset by a reduction

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:39.400
in overall claims.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.310
And payers are working
to adapt their plans

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:44.850
to cover telehealth.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:47.270
The pharma supply chains
are stretched thin,

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:51.100
and there's a need to transport
time sensitive COVID-19 tests

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:53.300
and vaccines around the world.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:54.790
And finally, the
industry is moving

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:57.390
to a virtual clinical trials.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.350
So an example of how
cloud AI is helping here,

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:04.700
is how a US hospital used
our Natural Language API

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:07.880
to analyze unstructured
data from patient inquiries

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:11.780
across multiple channels to more
accurately predict and triage

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:15.120
COVID-19 patients.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.990
Next, there's media,
entertainment, and gaming.

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:20.060
If your family is
anything like my family,

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:22.280
shelter in place policies
have increased media

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:24.460
streaming consumption
and gaming.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:27.470
But content production has
been paused in many cases,

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:30.530
with sports leagues, physical
productions, and major gaming

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:34.580
titles experiencing slowdowns
in production throughput.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.450
Because of the
slowdown in production,

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:39.500
it's more important than ever
to leverage existing content

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:42.560
and find flexible ways
to produce new content.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.660
And all of this like,
in other industries,

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:47.240
is placing additional
emphasis on cost efficiency

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:49.380
and flexibility.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:52.350
An example of how AI is
helping is the collaboration

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:54.600
between Google
Cloud and Fox Sports

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:58.170
to enable Fox's employees
to seamlessly search video

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:02.310
archives for specific footage
using artificial intelligence.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:04.410
By surfacing relevant
videos quickly,

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:07.350
media companies are able
to activate library content

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:08.700
faster.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.890
And also, as live
sports come back,

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:13.470
this capability
will allow producers

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.840
to more quickly
take library footage

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:17.955
and integrate it
with live clips.

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:25.010
The public sector at
all levels of government

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:27.140
is working to rapidly
modernize the delivery

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:30.080
of essential services,
as millions seek support

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:32.630
for unemployment, health care,
payroll, and public health

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:33.770
measures.

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:36.110
Government agencies and
academic institutions,

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:38.330
just like their counterparts
in the private sector,

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:40.760
are moving to digital platforms
and collaboration tools

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:42.669
to maintain operations.

00:08:42.669 --> 00:08:44.630
And amid this rapid
shift, there's

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:48.240
a continued focus on data
privacy and security.

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:51.588
Finally, like we talked about
in other areas of the economy,

00:08:51.588 --> 00:08:53.630
governments and schools
are facing cost pressures

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.910
and are being asked to
operate with efficiency

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:58.275
and flexibility.

00:08:58.275 --> 00:09:00.150
The state of New Jersey's
Department of Labor

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:01.650
worked with Google
Cloud to deploy

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:05.430
an AI-powered virtual chat
bot to provide real time

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:08.223
answers to the 20 most common
unemployment questions.

00:09:08.223 --> 00:09:10.890
And we'll talk through some more
examples from the public sector

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:13.370
later.

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:16.220
Now let's go into more detail
with some specific examples

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:19.220
where Google Cloud AI has
been partnering closely

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:21.690
with our customers.

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:24.060
I'll talk about three areas.

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:28.010
First, Contact Center AI,
including virtual agents.

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:31.040
Second, applying our
Lending AI solution

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:33.350
to the Paycheck
Protection Program.

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:35.660
And third, how new
features in Google Meet

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:38.913
have been supporting
remote work.

00:09:38.913 --> 00:09:41.330
First, let me share a quick
overview of our Contact Center

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:42.810
AI solution.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:46.560
Contact Center AI helps deliver
exceptional customer service

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.510
and increased
operational efficiency

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:50.760
using artificial intelligence.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:52.620
It does this in a few ways.

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:56.250
First, with Dialogflow, it
automates basic chat and voice

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:57.600
interactions.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.430
Next, with Agent
Assist, it makes

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:01.530
human agents more effective.

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:04.230
And third, with Contact
Center AI insights,

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:07.200
it unlocks insights about call
drivers and customer service

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.440
interactions.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:12.800
As the pandemic took hold and we
saw that many call centers were

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.800
becoming overwhelmed, our
Cloud AI teams quickly

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:18.740
built and implemented a
customized Contact Center AI

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:23.130
virtual agent to respond to
questions related to COVID-19.

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:24.990
The rapid response
virtual agent has

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:27.295
been deployed across
government and health care.

00:10:27.295 --> 00:10:29.670
I mentioned the state of New
Jersey's Department of Labor

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:31.030
earlier.

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:33.270
In addition, the state
of Illinois' Department

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:35.910
of Employment Security
also used this solution

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:37.890
to address
unemployment inquiries,

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:41.610
with more than 2.6 million voice
and chat interactions handled

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:43.870
by the virtual agent so far.

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:47.910
In health care, Penn Medicine
has enabled 24/7 access

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:50.880
to COVID-19 information
for concerned citizens

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:54.150
using this capability.

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:56.910
Next, Document AI
is a solution that

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:58.920
helps organizations
unlock insights

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.570
from their mountains
of documents

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:02.280
using artificial intelligence.

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:05.170
It turns unstructured
data into structured data,

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:09.470
which means you can now
understand it and utilize it.

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:12.080
In the United States, the
Small Business Administration's

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:14.330
Paycheck Protection
Program made funding

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:17.240
available to help businesses
keep their workforces employed

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:19.400
during the COVID-19 crisis.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:22.130
As you might expect, this
led to a massive increase

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:24.860
in loan applications that
needed to be processed.

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:27.410
Building on top of our
Document AI solution,

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:30.560
we created the Paycheck
Protection Program Parser

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:32.990
to enable lenders to use
artificial intelligence

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:36.110
to extract structured
information from loan documents

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:37.880
submitted by applicants.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:40.430
This can save time, can
be implemented quickly

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:43.250
and securely, and improves
the customer experience

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:47.260
by making the loan
process more efficient.

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:50.410
Finally, many of us are now
familiar with remote work

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:51.850
as the new normal.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.800
Our customers at Google
Cloud have not only

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:56.230
adopted video for
traditional team meetings,

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:59.060
but have also adopted
video for new use cases,

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:01.780
including virtual all
hands, frontline trainings,

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:03.363
and customer engagement.

00:12:03.363 --> 00:12:05.530
In fact, these are all ways
me and my team at Google

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:07.520
have used video just
in the past week,

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:11.260
and we see our customers
doing the same.

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:13.470
However, when you're
having a virtual meeting,

00:12:13.470 --> 00:12:16.200
there's nothing more distracting
than noise interference.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:18.990
Perhaps people chatting in
the background, a colleague

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:21.060
pounding on their keyboard
as they take notes,

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:23.030
or the shuffling of papers.

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:26.580
The Google Meet team has used
AI to limit these distractions

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:30.610
by intelligently filtering out
background noises in real time.

